  "narrative": {
    "intro": "TriWest Healthcare Alliance has $14.5B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. TriWest has 25 awards this fiscal year and an average award size of $581M. Obligations are up 8.6% year over year. Yearly obligations show a steady rise from $6.7B in FY21 to $14.5B in FY26. The Department of Veterans Affairs is the largest buyer at $9.8B, followed by the Department of Defense at $4.7B. Direct Health and Medical Insurance Carriers is the largest NAICS market at $14.2B, with Pharmacy Benefit Management and Other Third Party Administration of Insurance and Pension Funds at $288M. Current-year totals are partial, covering the fiscal year to date, and the note clarifies that listed award-value figures in largest-awards and expiring-contracts tables are total contract values while the other figures are contract obligations. This profile focuses on where obligations sit now, how award counts and sizes look this fiscal year, and which agencies and markets account for the bulk of TriWest’s federal work.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How has TriWest Healthcare Alliance’s federal business changed over recent years?",
        "body": "TriWest Healthcare Alliance reported obligations rising from $6.7B in FY21 to $14.5B in FY26. TriWest Healthcare Alliance obligations increased each year shown, reaching $13.4B in FY25 and $14.5B in FY26. TriWest Healthcare Alliance obligations are up 8.6% year over year for the current fiscal-year-to-date period."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Who are the main buyers and markets for TriWest Healthcare Alliance?",
        "body": "The Department of Veterans Affairs is the top buyer with $9.8B in obligations, and the Department of Defense follows with $4.7B. Direct Health and Medical Insurance Carriers is the largest market at $14.2B, and Pharmacy Benefit Management and Other Third Party Administration of Insurance and Pension Funds accounts for $288M."
      }
    ]
  },
